  - S&P 500
abstract: >-
  Code, data pipeline, and manuscript for a study of whether volatility
  persistence (rolling long-memory and roughness estimates on range-based
  variance) carries forecasting information as a shared market state beyond
  HAR and HAR-X benchmarks, on a panel of 115 S&P 500 stocks from November
  2001 to April 2026. Includes GPH and local-Whittle estimation, a layered
  forecasting ladder with panel-aware HLN-corrected Diebold-Mariano tests,
  and Moreira-Muir volatility-managed portfolio evaluation.
